Description: qmmf-server: wait for the CamX overlay before starting
 qti-cam-server.service gates startup on ExecCondition
 /usr/libexec/qmmf-server/check-camx-overlay.sh, which succeeds only when some
 /dev/video* node exists whose driver module name contains "camera". On QCS6490
 the camera_qcm6490 module is loaded asynchronously by udev from the device
 tree, so on a cold boot the condition can be evaluated before those nodes
 exist: measured on the Q6A (Ubuntu 26.04, kernel 7.0.11-7-qcom),
 systemd-modules-load finished at t=1s while camera_qcm6490 bound at t=6s, and
 the unit was evaluated at t=1s and skipped. A skipped unit is never retried,
 so qti-cam-server stayed down until it was started by hand. Evaluate the
 condition through a wrapper that polls for up to 60s, and order the unit after
 systemd-modules-load.service as the upstream unit intends.
Author: Radxa
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-13

